    <h1>ORUNKA Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><small>Effective {updated} · Applies to ORUNKA on iPhone and Mac (App Store) and Windows (Steam)</small></p>
    <p><strong>By default we collect no personal data.</strong> ORUNKA has no ads, analytics or tracking. Your game progress and settings are stored in files on your device. You can see the save location in Settings and erase it with “New game”; deleting the app removes it.</p>
    <p><strong>Optional cloud save.</strong> If you choose “Sign in” (with Apple or Google) on the title screen, we process your account ID (and, for Google, your email) to sign you in — Sign in with Apple does not request your name or email — and your save data (character name, level, pets, inventory, quest progress, play time), plus device type, game version and save time, so you can continue on other devices. This is stored in Google Firebase (Cloud Firestore and Authentication, Seoul region), is visible only to you and the developer, and is never sold, shared or used for ads. It is kept until you ask us to delete it — email us and we will delete your cloud save, backups and sign-in record. “Log out” turns cloud save off on that device only.</p>
    <p><strong>Optional multiplayer.</strong> While signed in, the game connects to our game server (game.seanson.com, Amazon Web Services, Seoul region) over an encrypted connection so other players can see you and chat. It processes your account ID, character name, level, position and pet appearance, chat messages, IP address, connection time, game version and device type. Position and appearance are shown to other players only while you are connected and are not stored. Connection logs and chat are kept on the server for up to 30 days for operations (abuse reports, troubleshooting) and then deleted.</p>
    <p>If Steam Cloud is enabled, save files may be synced by Valve under the <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/privacy_agreement/">Valve Privacy Policy</a>. Device backups on iPhone/Mac follow Apple’s policies.</p>
    <p>The game works offline. Only when cloud save is on does it upload and download your save over HTTPS. Sign-in happens via Apple or Google on hub.seanson.com; your password never reaches the game or the developer. Deleting a cloud save made with Sign in with Apple also revokes the app’s Apple sign-in. We do not knowingly collect children’s data and will delete a cloud save on a guardian’s request.</p>
